<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Durham, England</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Durham is a city in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> on a loop of the River Wear. It was founded in 995 when the community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-cuthbert">Saint Cuthbert</a> settled there with his relics, and its Norman cathedral, begun in 1093, and castle together form a World Heritage Site. For centuries it was the seat of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Durham, and its university was founded in 1832.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/durham-england.jpg" alt="Durham, England" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Benjamin Smith · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Durham_-_Cathedral_-_Exterior_-_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
